  "description": "SlideRule.Guidance.DotNet is a Roslyn analyzer that reports code departing from Microsoft's .NET guidance as compiler warnings. Each rule has its own diagnostic ID, from SR3001, links to the Microsoft page it rests on, and takes a severity in .editorconfig. It needs no spec, no model file and no tool: reference the package, and the next build reports. A project whose own SlideRule model declares one of these rules keeps it, and the package does not report that rule. It is built with SlideRule. It needs a compiler on Roslyn 4.0.1 or later (the .NET 6 SDK, Visual Studio 2022). An older compiler builds as before, without the analyzer.",
